{"type":"message","id":"ccf5c35a","parentId":"a597b976","timestamp":"2026-05-28T04:14:00.338Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Boss is saying that 3 other agents (Lucus, Codus, Wxlee) are not replying. These are other agents in Robot Space. Let me think about the context - this is a direct message from boss to me (Talus).\n\nSo \"他们\" = Lucus, Codus, Wxlee - these are other AI agents that are presumably in the Robot Space group chat, and they're not responding to messages.\n\nBoss is complaining that these other agents are not replying. This seems like a Robot Space group chat context issue.\n\nI should try to read the Robot Space group chat to see what's going on. But the message tool requires a messageId for reading... Let me think about what tools I have.\n\nI can try to get channel info or list messages somehow. But actually for Feishu, I might need to look at the feishu_post.py script to understand the group chat setup.\n\nActually - boss said in a DM to me that the other 3 agents aren't responding. This might be about the Robot Space group chat. \n\nLet me try to check if there's something going on with the other agents. But I don't have direct access to read group chat history without a messageId...\n\nWait, actually - I should ask boss for more context, or I could try to look at what's happening in the Robot Space group. But I'm in a direct message conversation with boss, so I don't have the group chat context here.\n\nThe most likely scenario: Boss is in Robot Space group chat, trying to reach Lucus/Codus/Wxlee (other agents), and they're not responding. Boss is telling me this as a complaint/observation.\n\nI should acknowledge and maybe ask what agents they are or if there's something specific boss wants me to do about it.\n","thinkingSignature":"bcd0c4ac4ac66e90ee98f11b8ceec8b4fa28866ad536d979e3ee103d6a607526"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n了解。Robot Space 群里其他三个 agent（Lucus、Codus、Wxlee）发消息都不回了。\n\n我能做什么？帮你@他们，还是你有其他想法