{"type":"message","id":"a7dc4d60","parentId":"cd6e5c49","timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:23:47.061Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue now. Looking at the bindings:\n- `lucus` → routes via `feishu` channel with `accountId: lucus`\n- `codus` → routes via `feishu` channel with `accountId: codus`\n- `wxlee` → routes via `feishu` channel with `accountId: xiaoye` (not directly)\n\nBut there's no binding for `wxlee` on feishu for the boss (ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff). Wxlee is only bound to `openclaw-weixin` (wechat) and `feishu` with `accountId: xiaoye`.\n \nSo the real problem is that Lucus, Codus, and Wxlee are all configured for different Feishu accounts or platforms entirely—they're not receiving the boss's messages in the first place. Rather than troubleshooting their individual configurations, I should probably use the Feishu wiki tool directly to access the document.\n","thinkingSignature":"70a2ec124ed0b9e153c950edc14522e4ede44595736500b9d190aa98177497b0"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_emiz4vw50zzy_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw && ls -la dist/plugins/feishu-wiki/ 2>/dev/null || find . -path '*feishu-wiki*' -name '*.js' 2>/dev/null | head -5","timeout":5}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":24342,"output":302,"cacheRead":41664,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":66308,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779974614895,"responseId":"066774d708136c54385fce26c44a833d"}}
