{"type":"message","id":"76937197","parentId":"7926c4ed","timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:24:55.183Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I notice from the config that feishu tools only has `doc: true` but not `wiki: true`. The feishu-wiki skill needs wiki tool enabled. Let me check if I can use the feishu_doc tool to read the wiki page directly - the wiki page content is stored as a doc in feishu.\n\nActually, looking at the feishu-wiki SKILL.md - it says the wiki tool is available but I need to check the config. The config shows `channels.feishu.tools.doc` is true, but I don't see wiki in there.\n\nWait, the skill file says:\n```\n## Configuration\n```yaml\nchannels:\n  feishu:\n    tools:\n      wiki: true # default: true\n      doc: true # required - wiki content uses feishu_doc\n```\n\n\nSo wiki is enabled by default. The issue is likely that the OpenClaw dist files aren't available, so I can't directly call the wiki tool through Node. Let me try using the feishu_doc tool directly to access the wiki page by its token, which should work if wiki support is enabled by default and doc is already set to true.\n\nActually, I need to get the obj_token first by calling feishu_wiki with action=get and the wiki token, then use that obj_token to read the document content.\n","thinkingSignature":"5fd7aac6612ccd0aa4a80b466a2635d0438c169d238baf89c2b25d017a0fcbf3"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n看到了——飞书工具配置只有 `doc: true`，没有 `wiki: true`。我先尝试用 doc 工具直接读取这个 wiki 页面的 obj_token，然后用 doc 读取内容。\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_u747sbfmz5v8_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw && node -e \"\n// Try loading the feishu plugin via openclaw's plugin system\nconst { execSync } = require('child_process');\ntry {\n  const r = execSync('openclaw tools list 2>&1', { timeout: 5000 });\n  console.log(r.toString());\n} catch(e) {\n  console.log(e.message);\n}\n\" 2>&1 | head -20","timeout":8}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-p