{"type":"message","id":"0ca3a75b","parentId":"474d9de6","timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:40:33.498Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's no actual token file. The feishu integration seems to work through the openclaw gateway, but when I try to call the Feishu API directly, there's no access token configured.\n\nActually, looking back at how the feishu channel works in OpenClaw - it's the gateway that handles all the feishu API calls. The tools like `feishu_wiki` and `feishu_doc` are called through the openclaw's internal tool system, not by me directly invoking curl with tokens.\n\nBut the feishu_wiki tool isn't available to me. Let me think about why. Looking at the config, the feishu plugin is enabled and the tools are configured (wiki: true, doc: true). But the tool itself isn't exposed to me as a callable function.\n\nActually wait - the user is saying \"给你开了 wiki:wiki 全权限\" - they've given me wiki:wiki full permissions. The tool should be available. But the SKILL.md says to use `feishu_wiki` tool, but I don't have that as a callable function. The tools I have access to are: read, write, edit, exec, process, cron, gateway, nodes, agents_list, sessions_list, sessions_history, sessions_send, sessions_spawn, sessions_yield, subagents, session_status, image, image_generate, music_generate, tavily_extract, tavily_search, tts, pdf, web_search, web_fetch, memory_get, memory_search, message.\n\nThe feishu_wiki and feishu_doc tools are not directly available to me as functions. They're probably called internally by the gateway when I use the `message` tool or something similar.\n\nWait - looking at the message tool, it has channel-specific actions for Feishu. But the SKILL.md for feishu-wiki says to use `feishu_wiki` tool, which I don't have. This might mean the feishu plugin tools are only available to agents that have the feishu channel explicitly configured, or they're only exposed in certain contexts.\n \nThe user is frustrated that I can't access their Feishu wiki even though they've granted full permissions, and they're right to be annoyed. The wiki tool simply isn't available as a callable function in my current context - it's not just a matter of permissions, but of tool availability itself.\n","thinkingSignature":"3f42073f0725b820657ad305bcebdad41ce003cb7aae4a015a7f41d173b88ff6"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n方法没问题，是工具本身就没注册到我这里。feishu_wiki 和 feishu_doc 这两个工具没给我用——不是因为权限，是因为 OpenClaw 的工具注册机制就这样。\n\n你直接粘贴内容，我读文本检查错误。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":153,"output":535,"cacheRead":51744,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":52432,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779975623823,"responseId":"066778c82d034a1ab53f18bc285f4f87"}}
