{"type":"message","id":"6abb78d1","parentId":"bdcfa6ec","timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:41:44.102Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The boss is asking how to add/configure the Feishu access token so that the feishu_wiki and feishu_doc tools can work. Let me think about this.\n\nLooking at the OpenClaw config, there's `channels.feishu` section. The feishu tools need an access token to call the Feishu API. The credentials file I found are just `allowFrom` files for authentication verification, not API tokens.\n\nFor Feishu wiki/doc access, OpenClaw typically uses the Bot authentication (app_access_token) or user access token. The config doesn't show a feishu access token anywhere.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to configure the feishu access token. Looking at the gateway config schema would help. Let me check `config.schema.lookup` for feishu-related config paths.","thinkingSignature":"5c233636724161af89eec11f9b9e10f8be6e42ac02643b4bf1791a8fbee9961e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_n53im4css61n_1","name":"gateway","arguments":{"action":"config.schema.lookup","path":"channels.feishu"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":809,"output":211,"cacheRead":51200,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":52220,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779975698631,"responseId":"066779130e2f43af20026e02bcbc864b"}}
