{"type":"message","id":"69490674","parentId":"1ecbb099","timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:41:50.471Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The schema doesn't have a `token` field for feishu channel. The feishu tool probably uses the appId/appSecret to get an access token automatically when needed. But the `feishu_wiki` and `feishu_doc` tools need to be registered in the tools section.\n\nActually, looking at the schema - there IS a `tools` section under `channels.feishu`. Maybe the wiki/doc tools need to be enabled there explicitly.\n\nBut the real issue is that my feishu plugin tools (`feishu_wiki`, `feishu_doc`) are registered by the openclaw feishu plugin but the plugin needs to be loaded from the right path. \n\nI think the better move is to stop trying to fetch the document directly - the user already has it open in Feishu and can copy-paste the content, or I can get the obj_token from the URL and work with that instead.\n","thinkingSignature":"3ca791613dc0dca728baf6c7f9a61a21d3fad2df326125772b4b1289d2413f5e"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nschema 里没有单独的 token 字段。token 应该是在飞书开放平台的应用里配置的，appId/appSecret 用来获取 access token。\n\n但问题是——我的 feishu_wiki 和 feishu_doc 工具根本就没注册进来，不是我缺 token。\n\n最简单的方法：**你去飞书打开那篇文档，直接复制全文贴过来**，比折腾工具快。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":2631,"output":271,"cacheRead":52000,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":54902,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779975704776,"responseId":"0667791912cf04b99fd3df0f02fb3772"}}
