{"type":"message","id":"5ee8e886","parentId":"c4025507","timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:41:59.887Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking if they need to login to OpenClaw. They might be asking about whether they need to do something with the wiki token in OpenClaw's web interface. But this doesn't quite make sense either.\n\nWait - maybe they mean logging into OpenClaw's web interface to configure the Feishu token/settings? Or maybe they're asking if the OpenClaw instance itself needs to be \"logged in\"?\n\nActually, re-reading the context: they said \"给你开了 wiki:wiki 全权限的\" (gave me wiki:wiki full permissions) - so they think they've already configured something. And now they're asking \"是要去 openclaw 登录一下么\" - asking if they need to login to openclaw.\n\n\nI'm not sure what OpenClaw's web login has to do with the Feishu API access issue though. Let me step back and clarify what they're actually asking about.\n","thinkingSignature":"f3788a4558a35cff5a242314f08f64124f8dcdd1ef6d7cb7e240ace1f57e5eb7"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n不是。OpenClaw 是个本地服务，不存在\"登录\"的问题。\n\n你的飞书 bot 已经有 appId/appSecret 的话，token 会自动获取。问题不是 token，是工具本身没注册进来。\n\n最最快的解法：你把文档内容复制粘贴过来我看一眼，比排查这个省时间。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":3062,"output":250,"cacheRead":51712,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55024,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779975714162,"responseId":"06677923020e4a0039184d3bb17b8cb9"}}
