{"type":"message","id":"7efc0137","parentId":"ceb40f55","timestamp":"2026-05-28T13:42:59.849Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is making a very valid point. If I can write to Feishu docs, I should be able to read them too. Let me look at what tools I have available for feishu doc writing.\n\nActually, the message tool with action=send can send messages to Feishu. But can I read? The message tool has action=read which requires messageId. Not the same as reading a doc.\n\nWait, the user is right. I have feishu_doc skill available which says it can read docs. But when I tried to use feishu_wiki, it wasn't registered. Let me check if feishu_doc is registered.\n\nActually, looking at the SKILL.md for feishu-doc, it says the tool is `feishu_doc`. But is that actually registered as a tool in my current session? The skills say they provide instructions, not necessarily that the tool is available.\n \nMaybe the issue is that the skill file exists but the actual `feishu_doc` tool isn't registered in my current runtime, or perhaps it's registered under a different name like `doc` or `feishu` instead.\n","thinkingSignature":"0cf79f05dc5d9b0deac4c2ae62fb5a4cd6947a2ba0f5932c8bec52c08985f348"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n你说得对。让我直接试：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_r81z2lbgrcs1_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw && cat > /tmp/test_wiki.js << 'EOF'\n// Try to use the feishu doc tool via the tool system\nconst { tools } = require('./dist/tools/index.js');\nconsole.log(Object.keys(tools).filter(k => k.includes('feishu') || k.includes('doc') || k.includes('wiki')));\nEOF\nnode /tmp/test_wiki.js 2>&1 | head -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":448,"output":368,"cacheRead":54464,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55280,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779975774038,