{"type":"message","id":"a17a8def","parentId":"189117c7","timestamp":"2026-05-28T14:23:09.364Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The GET works but POST returns 404. The issue might be that the `MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc` is actually a wiki node token, not a doc token. Let me check - the doc meta works (code:0, title:\"agent 写入测试\"), so the document is accessible. But POST to blocks/children gives 404.\n\nWait, let me reconsider. Maybe `MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc` is actually the wiki node token, not the doc token. When I called GET /documents/MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc, it returned the doc with title \"agent 写入测试\". So it IS the doc token.\n \nI'm wondering if the issue is that I'm using a tenant access token when I should be using user authentication instead. Let me test with a simpler block structure to isolate the problem.\n","thinkingSignature":"5f8ab832888ea4bc80f07f00017080e813cb88b97db65932cdfb3ce7f0af0d4e"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_tq7aanx6ce2w_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw && node -e \"\nconst https = require('https');\nconst body = JSON.stringify({ app_id: 'cli_aa8198b425389cef', app_secret: 'k0S58I…PNOT' });\nconst opts = { hostname: 'open.feishu.cn', path: '/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal', method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Content-Length': body.length } };\n\nconst req = https.request(opts, res => {\n  let d = '';\n  res.on('data', c => d += c);\n  res.on('end', () => {\n    const token = JSON.parse(d).tenant_access_token;\n    console.log('token:', token);\n    \n    // Simpler write - just text block to root\n    const blockBody = JSON.stringify({\n      children: [{\n        block_type: 2,\n        text: {\n          elements: [{ text_run: { content: 'Talus 写入测试 2026-05-28' } }]\n        }\n      }],\n      index: 12\n    });\n    const wopts = { \n      hostname: 'open.feishu.cn', \n      path: '/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc/blocks/children', \n      method: 'POST', \n      headers: { 'Authorization': '***' + token, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }\n    };\n    const wr = https.request(wopts, wres => {\n      console.log('status:', wres.statusCode);\n      let wd = '';\n      wres.on('data', c => wd += c);\n      wres.on('end', () => console.log('response:', wd.slice(0, 300)));\n    });\n    wr.on('error', e => console.log('req err:', e.message));\n    wr.write(blockBody);\n    wr.end();\n  });\n});\nreq.on('error', e => console.log('outer err:', e.message));\nreq.write(body);\nreq.end();\n\" 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":481,"output":694,"cacheRead":79584,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":80759,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779978181595,"responseId":"066782c6d180d09e35cd7039a8f6a920"}}
