{"type":"message","id":"7362bd19","parentId":"f8d5c9f7","timestamp":"2026-05-28T14:23:44.813Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The write API keeps returning 404 with \"invalid param\". Let me check the Feishu API documentation. The docx blocks API requires knowing the actual block IDs. I'm using `doxcnvuklhDQ7w3u6FBpARe4xZc` as parent, but that might be a folder/page block that doesn't accept children directly.\n\nLet me look at the actual block structure more carefully. The root doc block `MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc` has block_type 1 (doc). The second block `doxcnvuklhDQ7w3u6FBpARe4xZc` has block_type 3 (heading). \n\nThe `index: 12` parameter might be invalid since there are only 12 blocks total and the last one has a different parent. I should try writing to an existing paragraph block instead—`doxcnjy5CzMfQyuG9esM3mpPZWe` has block_type 2 (text). But actually, I think I'm calling the wrong endpoint. The correct API path for creating block children should be `/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/{document_id}/blocks/{block_id}/children` where `{block_id}` is the parent block.\n\nLooking at the response from the blocks query, the root block `MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc` has block_type 1, which is a doc container. The write API might expect the root block itself rather than trying to append to it. I'm also wondering if the issue is with how I'm constructing the JSON body—I need to make sure I'm formatting the block data correctly. Let me try the batch create endpoint with a different parent block. I think the problem might be the JSON structure itself - I should try creating a simpler paragraph block instead of that complex object.\n","thinkingSignature":"a08795802fe7caf7b19726678ab73b1356210f6b61986a20f50ce80ed1a34800"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_q5b6t6l0lgml_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw && node -e \"\nconst https = require('https');\nconst body = JSON.stringify({ app_id: 'cli_aa8198b425389cef', app_secret: 'k0S58I…PNOT' });\nconst opts = { hostname: 'open.feishu.cn', path: '/open-apis/auth/v3/tenant_access_token/internal', method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Content-Length': body.length } };\n\nconst req = https.request(opts, res => {\n  let d = '';\n  res.on('data', c => d += c);\n  res.on('end', () => {\n    const token = JSON.parse(d).tenant_access_token;\n    \n    // Try simple text block as child of root doc block\n    const blockBody = JSON.stringify({\n      children: [{\n        block_type: 2,\n        text: { elements: [{ text_run: { content: '--- Talus 写入测试 2026-05-28 14:21 UTC ---' } }] }\n      }]\n    });\n    // Use root doc block id as parent\n    const wopts = { \n      hostname: 'open.feishu.cn', \n      path: '/open-apis/docx/v1/documents/MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc/blocks/MKJtwW9nriMKh3kMmz4c3Bubnoc/children', \n      method: 'POST', \n      headers: { 'Authorization': '***' + token, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }\n    };\n    const wr = https.request(wopts, wres => {\n      let wd = '';\n      wres.on('data', c => wd += c);\n      wres.on('end', () => {\n        console.log('status:', wres.statusCode, 'code:', JSON.parse(wd).code, 'msg:', JSON.parse(wd).msg);\n      });\n    });\n    wr.write(blockBody);\n    wr.end();\n  });\n});\nreq.write(body);\nreq.end();\n\" 2>&1","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":672,"output":887,"cacheRead":81920,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":83479,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779978216856,"responseId":"066782e99456159ff605677754325d80"}}
